# Per-sleeve kill-switch — the SINGLE source of truth for which strategy sleeves run.
#
# Flip a sleeve to "off" and redeploy to retire it. Unlike `systemctl disable` by hand
# (which the next deploy silently re-enables), this SURVIVES deploys: the deploy enables
# only the "on" sleeves and `disable --now`s the "off" ones, and the verify + the liveness
# watchdog stop expecting them.
#
# SAFETY — what "off" does and does NOT do:
#   * "off" stops the sleeve's daemon -> NO NEW entries.
#   * It does NOT flatten open positions. Each open position keeps its Bybit-managed
#     server-side disaster stop AND ws_risk protection (the risk service always runs and
#     keeps reading every configured ledger root), so positions exit naturally with no
#     orphan/flatten risk. Wind a sleeve to flat BEFORE you consider it fully retired.
#   * The short sleeve's root is ws_risk's primary; turning SHORT off stops its entry
#     daemon but ws_risk still uses that root. The risk service itself has no toggle.
#
# Accepted values: on | off  (also 1/true/yes == on). Override per host in
# /etc/liquidity-migration/sleeves.env (sourced/loaded AFTER this file, so it wins).
#
# Plain KEY=value (no shell ${:-} expansion) so this file is valid as BOTH a bash `source`
# (deploy/verify) AND a systemd EnvironmentFile (the liveness watchdog reads the toggles to
# skip an intentionally-off sleeve). Keep it that way.

# SHORT  = liquidity-migration short (event_demo): the demo entry daemon — the REAL forward demo.
SHORT_SLEEVE=on
# SHORT_PAPER = the short sleeve's PAPER shadow (a no-order dry-run on its own ledger root; the
# daily paper<->demo reconcile arbiter). Split out of SHORT_SLEEVE so a small/low-RAM host can run
# the real forward demo WITHOUT the second full-universe paper process. OFF 2026-06-04 to fit a
# smaller box: reconcile.sh's paper<->demo leg goes quiet (demo<->backtest still works). Flip to
# on to restore the shadow. (Fallback default on a stripped checkout is on — see lib_sleeves.sh.)
SHORT_PAPER_SLEEVE=off
# LONG   = long-native v11a: demo + paper services. OFF 2026-06-04: retired to fit a smaller host.
# The long sleeve is a diversifier overlay (code-complete, not the core forward demo). "off" stops
# new long entries; open demo positions ride to natural exit under the always-on risk service (no
# flatten — wind to flat on Bybit first if you want a clean short-only book). Flip to on to restore.
LONG_SLEEVE=off
# CONTINUOUS = continuous-fade: demo + paper services + the daily rmom-refresh timer.
# OFF by default: the backtested edge was a ~25h rmom look-ahead (collapses to
# net-negative under the causal shift3 fix), disabled 2026-06-03 pending a genuinely
# causal signal. Versioned here (not just /etc) so a host rebuild can't resurrect it.
# Flip to on only after re-validation.
CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE=off
